  <p>Only <span style='color: var(--warning);'>≈ 45 %</span> of India’s net sown area is irrigated. The remaining <span style='color: var(--warning);'>≈ 55 %</span> depends on rain‑fed agriculture, making monsoon variability a critical risk factor for food security and military logistics (e.g., troop movement through flood‑prone plains).</p>
  
